# ==============================================================================
# .aiderignore
# Keeps Aider's repo map and token budget focused on active source code:
#   - core/           (C++ engine & gameplay logic)
#   - bridge/         (GDExtension Godot bindings)
#   - godot_project/  (Godot scenes, GDScript, shaders)
#   - tools/          (Python asset pipeline & extraction scripts)
#   - tests/          (Test suites)
#   - docs/ & plan/   (Design and architectural documentation)
#
# NOTE: You can still load any ignored file on demand in an Aider chat using:
#   /add <file>        (to edit or reference)
#   /read-only <file>  (to use as reference without edits)
# ==============================================================================

# --- 1. Extracted game assets (~4,300 sprites, audio, levels, images) ---
# Exclude all heavy asset files, but keep the top-level manifest accessible
extracted/*
!extracted/manifest.json

# --- 2. Bulk Ghidra 68k Mac decompilation archive (~1,560 raw C dumps) ---
# Raw reverse-engineering dumps are great reference material, but should be
# loaded on demand via `/read-only analysis/decomp/...` rather than auto-mapped.
analysis/decomp/
analysis/ghidra/

# --- 3. Gameplay recordings, clips, and visual references ---
media/

# --- 4. Scratch work, caches, and raw game rips ---
tmp/
qa_out/
hf-cache/
raw_game/
refs/

# --- 5. Temporary logs, diffs, and benchmark dumps in repo root ---
*.log
verify_out.txt
mech_out.txt
soi_shotlog.txt
soi_enemies_before.c
cmp.png
